<p>{% trans %}List formats control how many names are joined together. This is used for multi-value fields or lists like author names.{% endtrans %}</p>

<h2>{% trans %}Main choices{% endtrans %}</h2>
<ul>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Delimiter</strong>: Text between most names, such as a comma and space.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Last delimiter type</strong>: How to join the last two names, like "and".{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Delimiter precedes last</strong>: Choose never, always, or contextual behavior.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Reduce list and append et al</strong>: Shorten long lists after a limit.{% endtrans %}</li>
</ul>

<p>{% trans %}Example: "Jane Smith, John Lee, and Pat Kim".{% endtrans %}</p>
